WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.487
By the end of this module, you should be able to perform several connected data-cleaning tasks with S Q L.

00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:11.482
First, you should be able to profile a dataset.

00:00:11.482 --> 00:00:19.812
That means measuring missing values, blanks, placeholders, invalid values, and possible duplicates.

00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:24.482
Second, you should be able to standardize representations.

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:29.412
For example, you may normalize names, email addresses, phone numbers,

00:00:29.412 --> 00:00:34.984
or categories without pretending that an uncertain value is known.

00:00:35.696 --> 00:00:41.778
You should also be able to validate values using clear rules, identify duplicate groups,

00:00:41.778 --> 00:00:45.783
and apply an explicit rule when choosing a preferred record.

00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:49.943
Finally, you should know how to protect the original data.

00:00:49.943 --> 00:00:57.153
We will use views, transactions, returning results from updates, and database constraints.

00:00:57.153 --> 00:01:00.913
The larger goal is not just to write working SQL.

00:01:00.913 --> 00:01:07.246
You should be able to explain why each cleaning decision is reasonable and what uncertainty still remains.
